    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all 3 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional, region-validated `postcode` field to owners. Each piece went to the layer that owns that concern:\n\n**Contract / persistence**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional, `pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`); the generator flows it into `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` column, field, getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it both directions (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`), so it's stored and returned.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column (hsqldb is what the tests run against, which uses `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n**Reference data** (reused, not duplicated)\n- `Locality.java` already held the pinned city\u2192region table used by the mapper. I extended it with the region\u2192postcode-range table and a `postcodeAllowedForCity(city, postcode)` method that keeps the range array private. A city with no known region returns `true` (permissive).\n\n**Request handling** (OfficeFloor functions, per AGENTS.md)\n- New `ValidateOwnerPostcode` step: no-op when absent; rejects a non-4-digit value; then defers the region check to `Locality`. Wired into both the `POST /api/owners` and `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipelines, and `ApplyOwner` now sets postcode on update.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (mirrors the existing `InvalidTelephone` pair, reusing `ProblemDetails`) \u2192 400, plus its `officefloor/escalation/*.yml`.\n\n**Tests:** `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 valid postcode stored/returned, owner without postcode accepted (contract stays backward-compatible), malformed postcode rejected with 400. `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
